   - **Implementation exception:** `mano dev` and `mano build` are the two Mano actions allowed to write application code. Their complete authoritative contracts are `_mano/skills/dev.md` and `_mano/skills/build.md`, each plus the shared `_mano/rules/implement.md`. `mano dev` implements one story from `stories/README.md`; `mano build` works the Scope rows of `PHASE_DIR/progress.md` straight from the phase brief. A phase uses one path, never both. Preserve a literal trailing modifier: `mano dev yolo` and `mano-dev yolo` both invoke `mano-dev` with `yolo` intact, enabling the ordered batch mode defined in that contract. The planning-only refusal still applies to every other Mano action.
   <!-- /mano-rule: dev-yolo-batch -->

5. **Runtime Layout:**
   - In installed projects, Mano framework files live under `_mano/` even if the framework source repository stores them at the root.
   - When interpreting prompts or copied templates in a user project, prefer `_mano/skills`, `_mano/rules`, `_mano/templates`, and `_mano/custom` as the runtime paths.
